# DEPRECATED — this file does nothing.
#
# `.claudeignore` is NOT a Claude Code feature. It is not read, parsed, or
# honoured by any version of Claude Code; the old `ignorePatterns` setting it
# resembled was deprecated and replaced by the permissions system. This file was
# additionally inert because it sat in `markdown/` rather than the repo root.
#
# The real, supported mechanism is `permissions.deny` with `Read(...)` rules in
# project settings. Files matching a deny rule are excluded from file discovery
# and search results, and reads on them are refused.
#
#   ->  ../.claude/settings.json     (repo root — this is the file that works)
#
# Design note: deny rules are evaluated BEFORE allow rules and cannot carry
# allowlist exceptions, so the rules there are deliberately targeted at the
# heavy data directories (data/Tirupati, data/Wayanad, outputs/, the venvs) and
# binary extensions (*.tif, *.nc, *.pdf, *.png) rather than a blanket
# `Read(./data/**)` — a blanket rule would also hide the InSAR pipeline source
# in `data/wayanad_insar/*.py`, which must stay readable.
#
# Docs: https://code.claude.com/docs/en/settings
#       https://code.claude.com/docs/en/permissions
#
# This stub is kept only as a signpost. It is safe to delete.
